@jayyuen66/dsh-quality-gate README · <img src="https://api.iconify.design/lucide/plug.svg?color=%23658EFF&height=22" height="22" width="22" align="absmiddle" alt="" /> Enabling it in dsh：- Bundle form: `dsh.bundle.patch` in `package.json` points at `cordis.patch.yml`, which carries **two entries**: `- name: "@jayyuen66/dsh-plugin-shared"` (the supplier of the card components, deliberately **without an `id`** so the plugin page does not list it as a switchable component) and `- id: quality-gate` with `name` set to the bare package name (the host scans `dsh.client` only on bare-name entries); `dsh plugin --profile web add/remove` maintains those lines.
- The host half hard-depends only on `settings` (`default.inject = ["settings"]`); precedence is card runtime value > the line's `config:` > schema built-in defaults.
- The client half (`dsh.client.platform = web`, `immediately: true`) injects a card into the `plugins.bundle.config` slot of the plugin page. Two identifiers, deliberately different sources: the slot key is the **bundle package name** `@jayyuen66/dsh-quality-gate`, while the settings namespace and `configForms.get()` use the **bare entry id** `quality-gate` — mix them up

@jayyuen66/dsh-quality-gate README · <img src="https://api.iconify.design/lucide/terminal.svg?color=%23658EFF&height=22" height="22" width="22" align="absmiddle" alt="" /> The four gate commands：- `tsc` is only a logical name in the command: the entry is resolved at runtime — the project's own `typescript` first, then the copy shipped with this package, finally `tsc` on PATH (reported as not-run by the "tool unavailable" exit); never an `npx` auto-download.
- Root detection: from each edited file, up to `maxRootDepth` (default 10) levels to the nearest manifest root; a package that is **itself** a workspace root yielding `pnpm check` keeps its own root (a change in one package must not fan out into the whole umbrella workspace), and otherwise a monorepo package is upgraded to the workspace root holding `pnpm-workspace.yaml` — but only when that root **yields a gate**; otherwise the package keeps its own root (an outer workspace without a `check` script must not swallow the package's `tsc`/`ruff` gate).
